reviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7023035","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"36d474882e08b84124dad26b5410c4469f58a17c16c830d536b11f83b17dc8e2","compact":"21b4d6e3a537ad78168c062bfae945f273ec4433b9fa65a27eee8b6994f41dfa","nasal":"db4f9ffebe76cb92a1a856cedec83a5d312e1ec88b75deafdb61453d43448251"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-23-36","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":23,"verse":36,"english":"Having stretched their bows they pierced Mahodara, and then, all together they greatly angered prevented Rāvana.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.75,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-23-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7023036","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5d53f82a2798f7d2a31e8e7e59d0771a2f6677207bcfd26bf54a755f769e7ad5","compact":"0469ce971bd9222cf64327bc581e1ccb1a1c63b6bcf05b2ec2ba6b5da57c97a0","nasal":"0469ce971bd9222cf64327bc581e1ccb1a1c63b6bcf05b2ec2ba6b5da57c97a0"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-23-37","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":23,"verse":37,"english":"Thereupon the Ten-necked (demon), excited with wrath like the fire of dissolution, pierced them to their very vitals with highly dreadful arrows.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.651,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-23-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7023037","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1fe34be94d1fe76a207b49f12361c7c9d140171d04e1d03676529f458d7128b8","compact":"6838f17eee2d41009eba82831d4ad0b27ae6bded9321a3f56270a4fc2c9e7a30","nasal":"6838f17eee2d41009eba82831d4ad0b27ae6bded9321a3f56270a4fc2c9e7a30"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-23-38","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":23,"verse":38,"english":"And stationed above, he showered on them variegated maces, Bhallas* Pattisas, Saktis and huge ſataghnis. Though pierced through and through these valiant foot-soldiers rushed forth. *An arrow with a crescent-shaped head.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.711,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-23-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7023038","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"711dd98db8fd0611c084d5181b593da3755a040d75c78e1b698c7163b25233bb","compact":"b5dc0c3e8fd7760e0ffecede9efcd63bb65abd2d9119902ab74a1ea4459aefa7","nasal":"b5dc0c3e8fd7760e0ffecede9efcd63bb65abd2d9119902ab74a1ea4459aefa7"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-23-39","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":23,"verse":39,"english":"And stationed above, he showered on them variegated maces, Bhallas* Pattisas, Saktis and huge ſataghnis. Though pierced through and through these valiant foot-soldiers rushed forth. *An arrow with a crescent-shaped head.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.929,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-23-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7023039","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ecd3bf03eb1f3f2d0d349de053ab92b88e9e00f46ed3e6b42babb74234bf5321","compact":"1164e3e6812ac7c735689fc0b2e91ca0594233b0834a489b410d6cd59fbc7ea2","nasal":"1164e3e6812ac7c735689fc0b2e91ca0594233b0834a489b410d6cd59fbc7ea2"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-23-40","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":23,"verse":40,"english":"Thereupon emitting loud cries the Rākşasa, like to a cloud, with a downpour of diverse shafts, destroyed the offspring of Varuna.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.696,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-23-38"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7023040","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"709afa626526f756246c521fbc50756734c906b742aa90610c43c07563439cd2","compact":"aaeffcc1ff6dd758c3c4bd38158b958d7915b9943ee8f0d3900b00a041c43da6","nasal":"a2